mallet_speed_m_s	1.0
duration_s	4.0
substeps	32
rate_hz	48000
full_scale_pa	2.0
# MODE CERTIFICATE: maximum_relative_halfwidth 1e-6, the largest value the engine accepts for this row. At the earlier card's 1e-7 the first scan of the engine cut solve, on the start cut, was refused in window 1 of the 8-window plan, on the mode at 365.752 Hz, f1 on that cut: relative half-width 6.19e-6 (FS-MODAL-HALFWIDTH-EXCEEDED); the scan was stopped before its other window counts ended. A relative half-width is the eigenvalue's, so at f1 that is 1.1e-3 Hz, 0.0054 c, and the 1e-6 row bounds it at 1.8e-4 Hz (2.2e-4 Hz at 442 Hz), 0.00087 c: a window count certifies the cut only where every half-width lies under 1e-6. It sets no sound. 1e-6 is the next decade, as 1e-8 to 1e-7 was on the marimba and xylophone cards.
maximum_relative_halfwidth	1e-6
tube	closed_open
tube_radius_m	0.023
tube_air_length_m	0.177000
tube_gap_m	0.0127
tube_modes	4
# RECEIVER: the broadband observer (e6313e19d): one delay and an order-16 rational fit of the boundary-element transfer from each bar mode to the receiver, checked on held-out frequencies against a 5 % budget. It hears the bar during the mallet's contact and with its travel time; the narrow-band law it replaces passed the contact force as a pulse.
observer	broadband
observer_fit_order	16
observer_held_out_budget	0.05
observer_rigid_rows	on
